/-! # X5 connector: equation preservation under the 36-element symmetry

The support system for orbit `01,02,03,04,15` has 75 variables and 675
polynomials; every monomial has degree three with coefficient one, and exactly
three polynomials carry the constant `-1`.  Each group element induces a
permutation of the variables; the tables below additionally supply, as an exact
witness, the permutation of polynomial indices it induces.  `system_preserved`
checks in the kernel that renaming the variables of polynomial `i` by element
`g` yields precisely polynomial `polyPerm (g, i)`, and the two inverse tables
certify that both permutations are bijections.  Hence every element maps the
polynomial system onto itself. -/

